From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Schmiedel <Martin.Schmiedel@tq-group.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: freescale: fsl-samsung-hdmi: keep runtime PM active

A hdmi_pclk rate change holds clk_prepare_lock and resumes the PHY
through clk_pm_runtime_get(). If the PHY suspends at the same time, the
resume waits for the suspend. The suspend takes clk_prepare_lock in the
PHY driver and in imx8mp_blk_ctrl_power_off(). Both tasks block.

Keep the runtime PM reference from probe. The PHY no longer suspends at
runtime. System suspend and resume still use the callbacks.

Signed-off-by: Martin Schmiedel <Martin.Schmiedel@tq-group.com>
---

diff --git a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c
index 191c282..8c823a9 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-samsung-hdmi.c
@@ -671,8 +671,11 @@
 		goto register_clk_failed;
 	}
 
-	pm_runtime_put(phy->dev);
-
+	/*
+	 * Keep the runtime PM reference: a hdmi_pclk rate change holds
+	 * clk_prepare_lock and would wait for a running suspend, which takes
+	 * clk_prepare_lock here and in the power domain.
+	 */
 	return 0;
 
 register_clk_failed:
@@ -682,6 +685,7 @@
 static void fsl_samsung_hdmi_phy_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	of_clk_del_provider(pdev->dev.of_node);
+	pm_runtime_put_noidle(&pdev->dev);
 }
 
 static int __maybe_unused fsl_samsung_hdmi_phy_suspend(struct device *dev)
